  "what": "Every HOST TO = OFTO row of the TEC register vintage below, with the side of B6 it implies, checked by hand.",
  "why": "OFTO names an offshore transmission owner, not a geography: the licence says nothing about which side of the Anglo-Scottish boundary the export cable lands. 015's ladder put SHET and SPT north and NGET south and left OFTO in neither set, so a unit that matched an OFTO row was silently left ungraded (defect D3). The side is therefore taken from the row's onshore landfall, one row at a time, and only from this file.",
  "scope": "This enumeration is valid for the vintage named below and for no other. A register vintage whose OFTO set has not been enumerated and checked this way yields unknown, never south. Note that in this vintage every Scottish offshore project (Beatrice, Moray East, Moray West, Seagreen, Inch Cape, Neart na Gaoithe, Kincardine, Hywind, Aberdeen) is hosted by SHET or SPT, not by OFTO, which is why all 15 OFTO rows here land in England or Wales. That is an observed fact about this vintage, not a property of the OFTO licence.",
